\ Strict-mode rejection of `cond`: branch-combinator over a runtime
\ branches array. The body dispatches on a quotation pulled from the
\ array at runtime, so the AOT compiler cannot specialize the
\ row-variable effect. Calling `cond` from compiled code must surface
\ as a build error in --interpreter-fallback=false mode, naming
\ `cond` as the compound callee.
{ [ t ] [ "match" print-line ] } cond
